[gd_scene load_steps=17 format=3]

; BUBBLE BAY — the second official world (REQ-028), and the deliberate
; opposite of Coral Cove wherever the Level Contract offers a choice:
;   * NO boss — proving a world declaring none stays valid and completable
;     (the optional-boss path is an acceptance criterion here, not a cut),
;   * NO tuningOverrides — the restoration economy runs on the DEFAULT costs
;     (5 to reach resourced + 8 to reach restored = thirteen pearls), so the
;     absent-optional-element default path is exercised by an official world,
;   * the JET mod — the one Gill Mod Coral Cove does not emphasize, so the
;     official set requires all three MVP mods between its two worlds.
; Like Coral Cove it is manifest + scene with NO scripts: every mechanic is a
; scene-group + metadata declaration the WorldSystems runtime binds.
;
; THE ROUTE (one straight line down -Z, drivable with a single held forward
; key, because completability is a headless test, not a hope):
;
;   z   2  spawn (land — waddle)
;   z  -6  the bay: a WaterVolume across the route — water grammar
;   z -18  back onto land (grammar returns)                 [checkpoint 1]
;   z -24  Jet Gill Mod pickup
;   z -28  JET GATE — a wrecked trawl net, open only while the equipped mod
;          grants `jet_dash`. Mandatory: it spans the full route, and it is
;          the traversal challenge Coral Cove does not gate on.
;   z -32                                                   [checkpoint 2]
;   z -34..-52  thirteen pearl pickups — restoration resources for region
;          `kelp_nursery` at the contract's DEFAULT costs (no overrides)
;   z -55  NURSERY BOOM — the region's declared traversal gate; opens when
;          `kelp_nursery` reaches `restored`. Restoration is MANDATORY.
;   z -59  finish volume — reach_volume returns the player to the lagoon.
;
; CHECKPOINT DENSITY follows REQ-003 AC-7: the replay from any anchor to the
; next must fit progression.max_retry_seconds (5 s) at normal traversal, so
; six checkpoints sit at z -10, -20, -26, -32, -41, -50 — and the bubble
; walk MEASURES every segment rather than trusting this comment.

